    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-70064",
      "knowledge_point_id": "aa2418a8-b245-5600-8e7e-c54506e3f321",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Dimensions of the Transpose of a Matrix",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix\n    $L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 1 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${L}^{T}?$",
      "worked_solution": "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $m\\times n$ to $n\\times m.$\n\nSo, since $L$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, the transpose ${L}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix.",
